{"nodes": [{"id": "adr_0014_compose_not_kubernetes", "label": "ADR-0014 Docker Compose replicas; Kubernetes deliberately excluded", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/architecture/adr/0014-compose-not-kubernetes.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "adr_0014_compose_not_kubernetes_compose_replicas", "label": "Three-replica Compose demo behind nginx", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "The lesson is that process-local state does not survive multiple instances, and Compose shows it in about 30 seconds with a file anyone can read end to end. Accepted: Compose is not production (no rolling deploys, health routing, autoscaling or self-healing), and the demo has never been executed here \u2014 no Docker daemon, so the files are only `docker compose config`-validated.", "source_file": "docs/architecture/adr/0014-compose-not-kubernetes.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "adr_0014_compose_not_kubernetes_kubernetes_rejected", "label": "Kubernetes (rejected)", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Adds enormous operational surface and not one concurrency insight \u2014 manifests, a local cluster, an ingress controller and an image registry before the same demonstration. It would also mislead by implying scaling is a Kubernetes topic. Kubernetes is warranted for operational properties (rolling deploys, self-healing, autoscaling, service discovery), never to make code fast.", "source_file": "docs/architecture/adr/0014-compose-not-kubernetes.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "adr_0014_compose_not_kubernetes_nginx_round_robin", "label": "nginx round-robin (not sticky)", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Breaks SignalR across replicas; documented rather than fixed with sticky sessions, because finding it yourself is more instructive than having it silently handled.", "source_file": "docs/architecture/adr/0014-compose-not-kubernetes.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "adr_0014_compose_not_kubernetes_instance_id", "label": "INSTANCE_ID per service", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Injected per service and returned by /api/health and the scale endpoints, so you can see which replica served each request.", "source_file": "docs/architecture/adr/0014-compose-not-kubernetes.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "adr_0014_compose_not_kubernetes_hot_account_k6", "label": "loadtests/k6/hot-account.js", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "The script that exposes the in-process lock, because it drives concurrent requests through nginx \u2014 the lab's own runner drives all actors from within one instance and therefore cannot show the failure.", "source_file": "docs/architecture/adr/0014-compose-not-kubernetes.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "adr_0014_compose_not_kubernetes", "target": "adr_0014_compose_not_kubernetes_compose_replicas", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture/adr/0014-compose-not-kubernetes.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "adr_0014_compose_not_kubernetes_compose_replicas", "target": "adr_0014_compose_not_kubernetes_kubernetes_rejected", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture/adr/0014-compose-not-kubernetes.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "adr_0014_compose_not_kubernetes_compose_replicas", "target": "adr_0014_compose_not_kubernetes_nginx_round_robin", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture/adr/0014-compose-not-kubernetes.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "adr_0014_compose_not_kubernetes_compose_replicas", "target": "adr_0014_compose_not_kubernetes_instance_id", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture/adr/0014-compose-not-kubernetes.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "adr_0014_compose_not_kubernetes_hot_account_k6", "target": "adr_0012_postgres_advisory_locks_inprocessaccountlock", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture/adr/0014-compose-not-kubernetes.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "adr_0014_compose_not_kubernetes_nginx_round_robin", "target": "adr_0009_signalr_for_live_timeline_backplane", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture/adr/0014-compose-not-kubernetes.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "adr_0014_compose_not_kubernetes_compose_replicas", "target": "adr_0004_hybrid_persistence_inmemoryaccountstore", "relation": "references", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "docs/architecture/adr/0014-compose-not-kubernetes.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "adr_0014_compose_not_kubernetes", "target": "adr_0015_local_postgres_over_testcontainers", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture/adr/0014-compose-not-kubernetes.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}], "hyperedges": []}